====================================================================
  OVERALL FINDINGS TABLE
====================================================================
  saved table: Table_FINDINGS_overall_v9.csv
  - Nature of these exhibits: Illustrative firm-level case studies, NOT statistical tests.
      => Use to build mechanism intuition; cite phases 4/6/8 for inference.
  - Confirming cases: Nike (apparel) and Philips (med devices, NL): inventory build then margin fell.
      => Illustrate the H1 mechanism in significant/illustrative sectors.
  - Honest counter-case (Align): DIO rose 33→114 days yet premium gross margin held 71-76%.
      => Signal is probabilistic, not deterministic — included deliberately to avoid cherry-picking.
  - Semiconductors reframed: Vivid firm cases (Micron, Intel) but sector effect p=0.36, NOT significant.
      => Firm-level vividness does not equal a sector effect; v8 "semis" story does not replicate.
  - International coverage: Cases span 6 countries (US, NL, DK, DE, GB); Philips/Burberry/Ahold are non-US.
      => Demonstrates the signal is not a US-only artifact at the firm level.
  - Roster honesty (Table 25): "Played out?" column spans yes / partial / flat / NO.
      => Realistic mix, not a string of confirmations.

